All 15 tests now pass. Here's a summary of the 10 bugs I fixed across `src/`:

**`src/auth.py`** (3 bugs)
1. `has_permission` — compared roles case-sensitively. Fixed to compare lowercase versions.
2. `is_admin_or_owner` — used `and` instead of `or`; ownership should grant access even without the admin role.

**`src/inventory.py`** (4 bugs)
3. `__init__` — stored the mutable default dict directly, causing shared state across instances. Fixed with `dict(initial)`.
4. `add` — overwrote the existing quantity instead of accumulating. Fixed to `+=`.
5. `reserve` — used `>=` instead of `>`, rejecting the valid case of reserving exactly the available amount.
6. `release` — allowed releasing more than was reserved, producing negative counts instead of raising `ValueError`.

**`src/text_utils.py`** (3 bugs)
7. `slugify` — preserved uppercase letters; fixed to lowercase alphanumeric characters.
8. `slugify` — `replace("--", "-")` only collapses one pair of dashes. Added a `while` loop to collapse all consecutive separators.
9. `truncate` — returned `text[:max_len] + suffix`, exceeding `max_len`. Fixed to truncate to `max_len - len(suffix)` before appending the suffix.
